cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AI Law Atlas"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below. Please also cite AGORA (Emerging Technology Observatory) when using AGORA-derived records."
type: dataset
abstract: "A registry of 1,574 laws, regulations and bills governing artificial intelligence and its inputs (data, compute, chips, data centers, energy) from 57 countries and blocs, with structured annotations of 770 of them: dated events, thresholds, obligations, sanctions, definitions and relations, each with its provision and a verbatim quote. Annotated by Claude Haiku 5.5 and validated with a blinded protocol (Tier A item precision 93%, recall 96%). Research data, not legal advice."
authors:
  - family-names: "Covarrubias"
    given-names: "Matías"
version: "1.0.1"
date-released: "2026-10-14"
license: CC-BY-4.0
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23374030"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MatiasCovarrubias/ai-law-atlas"
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - regulation
  - legal data
  - data centers
  - natural experiments
